From 3489f1d9997e243eca501ec3a93f38772030b1c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 10:31:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02543/11362] [outer-loop] object-centric repr: confirmed
 representation was the blocker for MOVEMENT games (cn04/sp80)

The decisive test the other three probes pointed at: is the dynamics' pixel-level
messiness a property of the GAMES or of the REPRESENTATION? Segment each frame into
objects (connected non-bg components) and measure whether the dynamics become clean
object operations. Caught + corrected my own metric over-claim mid-probe: a naive
shape-only rearrangement rate scored RECOLOR/toggle games 'clean' though no object
moves -- so the final metric SPLITS movement vs recolor and computes object-cleanliness
only over MOVEMENT transitions.

RESULT (results/arc3_object_centric_repr.json):
  - REPRESENTATION WAS THE BLOCKER for movement games: sp80 (70/70 movement transitions =
    clean single-object translations) and cn04 (50/95) were exact-match 0 at the PIXEL
    level but decompose into clean object translations at the OBJECT level. Confirmed.
  - ar25 partial (0.35; reflect + selection-recolor mix); cd82 movement-but-not-clean (0.0).
  - RECOLOR/TOGGLE is a DISTINCT clean primitive class: ka59/sc25/tu93/sk48 are ~100%
    in-place recolor (verified: 0% background-involving change) -- not movement; the bridge's
    primitive library must include recolor/toggle, not just translate/reflect/push.
  - SEGMENTATION must be COLOR-AWARE: connectivity-only fails on m0r0 (one ~1840px blob).

SYNTHESIS across all four probes tonight: seeding fixed the data-front but engine accuracy
was the wall; whole-engine transfer was 0 even for similar games; a translation primitive
fit 0 games at pixel level; and here, at the OBJECT level, movement games become clean. The
binding constraint was the STATE REPRESENTATION. The offline->live bridge that follows:
object-centric perception (color-aware segmentation) -> a small primitive library
(translate/reflect/push + recolor/toggle) -> per-game params fit from a few live observations.
That is live-legal (no internet), transfers as a SKILL+vocabulary (not as reused engines),
and is the empirically-derived architecture for unseen ARC-AGI-3 games. Adversarial-verify: clean.

